Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:26:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Scope InputDeviceCapabilities to target window for
 focus events

FlyWeb pending: from branch-heads/8078 7e5aab9f6a. Applied after pendiente/chromium/0003;
applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> Scope InputDeviceCapabilities to target window for focus events
>
> InputDeviceCapabilities instances are maintained per DOMWindow to ensure
> they match the document context. During sequential focus navigation
> across frames, FocusController::AdvanceFocusInDocumentOrder passed the
> starting window's source_capabilities directly to Element::Focus() in a
> different document, which then exposed it as
> FocusEvent.sourceCapabilities in that document.
>
> This change updates AdvanceFocusInDocumentOrder to resolve
> source_capabilities using the target element's DOMWindow before focusing
> it. In addition, the FocusEvent constructor now always resolves
> source_capabilities to the object owned by the event's view (or null if
> there is no view), so no other path can expose another window's
> InputDeviceCapabilities object through a focus event.
>
